@startuml
!include ../../_style.iuml
' Derived from crates/openmeet-engine/src/integrity.rs (OpenAnswer, on_candidate_segment, on_candidate_speech_started,
' on_timer, finalize_answer, prepare_check, spawn_integrity_check, run_integrity_check, store_integrity_flag),
' crates/openmeet-engine/src/conversation.rs (IntegrityTimer), crates/openmeet-core/src/integrity.rs (IntegrityFlag,
' IntegrityLevel). The state belongs to the open answer; the stored IntegrityFlag is its latest revision.
title State of one candidate answer's integrity flag (interviewer mode)

[*] --> Collecting : first candidate utterance\n(on_candidate_segment creates OpenAnswer)

state Collecting {
  [*] --> Speaking
  Speaking : candidate speaking; timer version bumped\non each speech start (old timer outdated)
}

state "Pausing" as Pausing : turn-end timer armed\n(turn_end_silence_ms, default 1500 ms)\nfires only for the latest version

Collecting --> Pausing : utterance final\n(timer armed with version)
Pausing --> Collecting : candidate speaks again\n(on_candidate_speech_started)

state "Checking (revision n)" as Checking : Background request IntegrityCheck\nfour signals run in parallel\n(delivery computed before)
Pausing --> Checking : timer fires, candidate silent,\nunits not yet checked\n(on_timer -> CheckJob)

Checking --> Checked : fused and stored\nIntegrityChecked emitted
Checking --> Checking : newer revision starts\n(previous ticket cancelled,\nits flag is never stored)
Checking --> Cancelled : emergency stop or\nmeeting closed while running

state "Checked (revision n)" as Checked : flag stored and shown\nlevel low / possible / high / unavailable
Checked --> Collecting : candidate continues\n(same answer id, next revision)

state Final : closed answer: last check done;\nthe answer joins the delivery baseline\n(first 3 answers with at least 10 words)

Collecting --> Final : next interviewer question\nor meeting ends (finalize_answer)
Pausing --> Final : finalize_answer, unchecked units:\nlast check (last = true) first
Checked --> Final : finalize_answer, all units checked:\nbaseline commit only
Cancelled --> Final : answer closed
Final --> [*]

note right of Checked
  A flag is a signal for the interviewer,
  never a verdict. Revisions only grow;
  a stale revision never replaces a newer one.
end note

note bottom of Final
  The flag row in integrity_flags keeps the
  last stored revision (replaced by id).
end note
@enduml
